From 0380b4c52ee6daefd3e32dfb629a71b92965596c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carson Daniel <wcarsond@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:29:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] ggml: GGML_TYPE_Q12H - lossless 12.875-bit storage for
 bf16 weights

256-weight blocks of 412 bytes: lut[16] of the block's most frequent bf16
exponent bytes, 4 fixed exception slots (epos/eval, 0xFF = empty), nib[128]
of 4-bit lut indices and sm[256] of sign<<7|mantissa. Reconstruct with
u16 = (sm>>7)<<15 | lut[nib]<<7 | (sm&0x7F), overwrite the exceptions,
f32 = u16<<16. 12.875 bpw, r = 0.805 against bf16.

Enum 43 (GGML_TYPE_COUNT 44), GGML_FTYPE_MOSTLY_Q12H 29,
LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_Q12H 42, gguf-py GGMLQuantizationType.Q12H 43.

CPU path only: vec_dot_type is GGML_TYPE_F32 so src1 needs no conversion,
and ggml_vec_dot_q12h_f32 dequantizes a block into a local buffer and
accumulates. Correct, not fast. No CUDA or Vulkan shader yet - those
backends decline the type and the ops fall back to the CPU.

Q12H is lossless, so llama_tensor_get_type_impl returns early for this
ftype (output and token_embd stay Q12H, no Q6_K promotion) and the
shape fallback is BF16 rather than Q4_0.

Validated on Qwen3-1.7B (2,031,616,000 weights, 7,936,000 blocks):
quantize -> dequantize bitwise exact both through a numpy decode of the
on-disk blocks and through a Q12H -> BF16 requantize with ggml's own
dequantizer; file ratio 0.804997; greedy output identical to the bf16
GGUF at -n 64 and -n 256 on CPU. Worst block used 1 of the 4 exception
slots (one block in 7.9M).
